  "correct": "3",
  "solution": "The logic followed here is as shown below:\n\n**(1st number - 2nd number)⁴ = 3rd number**\n\nGiven, \n\n(23, 25, 16) \n\n⇒ (23 - 25)⁴ = 16\n\n⇒ **(2)⁴ = 16**\n\n(21, 17, 256)\n\n⇒ (21 - 17)⁴ = 256\n\n⇒ **(4)⁴ = 256**\n\nNow checking the options,\n\n1. (14, 19, 125)\n\n⇒ (14 - 19)⁴ = 125\n\n⇒ (5)⁴ = 125\n\n⇒ **625 ****≠ 125**\n\n2. (27, 23, 64)\n\n⇒ (27 - 23)⁴ = 64\n\n⇒ (4)⁴ = 64\n\n⇒ **256 ****≠ 64**\n\n3. (18, 15, 81)\n\n⇒ (18 - 15)⁴ = 81\n\n⇒ (3)⁴ = 81\n\n⇒ **81 = 81**\n\n4. (11, 9, 12) \n\n⇒ (11 - 9)⁴ = 12\n\n⇒ (2)⁴ = 12\n\n⇒ **16** ≠ 12\n\nHence, the correct answer is '**option 3)'.**",
